        "text": "All the required Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] `register_user.py` - creates a new email/password user account using AWS Cognito.\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] `email_password_login.py` - signs in a user with email and password and returns tokens using AWS Cognito.\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] `refresh_session.py` - refreshes an expired session or access token using AWS Cognito.\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] `password_reset.py` - starts a password reset flow for a local account using AWS Cognito.\n5. [HELPER] `identity_client.py` - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Email/Password Account Lifecycle using AWS Cognito.\n6. [HELPER] `identity_models.py` - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Email/Password Account Lifecycle.\n7. [LATER-STEP] `welcome_translate.py` - Translates onboarding copy into the user's locale using AWS Translate.\n8. [LATER-STEP] `profile_moderation.py` - Moderates profile text before account activation using AWS Comprehend.\n9. [LATER-STEP] `onboarding_summary.py` - Summarizes onboarding state for support using AWS DynamoDB.\n10. [LATER-STEP] `profile_note_store.py` - Persists onboarding notes and support metadata in a managed document store using AWS DynamoDB.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses a concrete external provider (AWS) and makes that provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
